n   131→\n   132→        .release-date {\n   133→            color: #828282;\n   134→            font-size: 11px;\n   135→        }\n   136→\n   137→        .empty-section {\n   138→            color: #828282;\n   139→            font-style: italic;\n   140→            padding: 20px;\n   141→            text-align: center;\n   142→        }\n   143→\n   144→        .footer {\n   145→            max-width: 1200px;\n   146→            margin: 30px auto 0;\n   147→            padding: 15px 0;\n   148→            border-top: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n   149→            text-align: center;\n   150→            color: #828282;\n   151→            font-size: 12px;\n   152→        }\n   153→\n   154→        .footer a {\n   155→            color: #828282;\n   156→        }\n   157→\n   158→        .footer a:hover {\n   159→            color: #ff6600;\n   160→        }\n   161→\n   162→        .highlight {\n   163→            background-color: #fff6e5;\n   164→            padding: 2px 4px;\n   165→            border-radius: 2px;\n   166→        }\n   167→\n   168→        .count {\n   169→            display: inline-block;\n   170→            background-color: #ff6600;\n   171→            color: #ffffff;\n   172→            padding: 2px 8px;\n   173→            border-radius: 10px;\n   174→            font-size: 11px;\n   175→            font-weight: bold;\n   176→            margin-left: 8px;\n   177→        }\n   178→\n   179→        @media (max-width: 1024px) {\n   180→            .container {\n   181→                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n   182→            }\n   183→\n   184→            .container .column:nth-child(3) {\n   185→                grid-column: 1 / -1;\n   186→            }\n   187→        }\n   188→\n   189→        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n   190→            .container {\n   191→                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n   192→            }\n   193→\n   194→            .container .column:nth-child(3) {\n   195→                grid-column: auto;\n   196→            }\n   197→\n   198→            .header h1 {\n   199→                font-size: 20px;\n   200→            }\n   201→        }\n   202→\n   203→        @media print {\n   204→            body {\n   205→                background-color: #ffffff;\n   206→            }\n   207→\n   208→            .column {\n   209→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   210→            }\n   211→\n   212→            a {\n   213→                color: #000000;\n   214→            }\n   215→\n   216→            a::after {\n   217→                content: \" (\" attr(href) \")\";\n   218→                font-size: 10px;\n   219→                color: #828282;\n   220→            }\n   221→        }\n   222→    </style>\n   223→</head>\n   224→<body>\n   225→    <header class=\"header\">\n   226→        <h1><span class=\"accent\">Agentic Coding</span> Research Report</h1>\n   227→        <div class=\"date\">April 6, 2026 — Daily updates on AI coding agents, tools, and insights</div>\n   228→    </header>\n   229→\n   230→    <main class=\"container\">\n   231→        <section class=\"column\">\n   232→            <div class=\"column-header\">\n   233→                New Products <span class=\"count\">26</span>\n   234→            </div>\n   235→\n   236→            <div class=\"item\">\n   237→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/andeya/codineer\" target=\"_blank\">Codineer</a></div>\n   238→                <div class=\"item-description\">Your local AI coding agent — one binary, zero cloud lock-in. Built in safe Rust, ships as a single binary with no daemon and no cloud dependency.</div>\n   239→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   240→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   241→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   242→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-03</span>\n   243→                </div>\n   244→            </div>\n   245→\n   246→            <div class=\"item\">\n   247→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Fengsh0923/Memocore\" target=\"_blank\">Memocore</a></div>\n   248→                <div class=\"item-description\">Agent Universal Memory Layer with persistent, self-healing memory. Built on Graphiti + Neo4j with Claude Code hook integration.</div>\n   249→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   250→                    <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   251→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   252→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-03</span>\n   253→                </div>\n   254→            </div>\n   255→\n   256→            <div class=\"item\">\n   257→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/LocalKinAI/kin-code\" target=\"_blank\">Kin Code</a></div>\n   258→                <div class=\"item-description\">Lightweight AI coding assistant for your terminal written in Go. Single 10MB binary with zero dependencies. Features MCP support and Soul files for custom AI personas.</div>\n   259→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   260→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   261→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   262→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-02</span>\n   263→                </div>\n   264→            </div>\n   265→\n   266→            <div class=\"item\">\n   267→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/iabhisekbosepm/custom_agent\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Agents</a></div>\n   268→                <div class=\"item-description\">Terminal-based AI coding assistant running entirely on your machine with 5 specialized agents (explorer, coder, reviewer, documenter, architect) and 35+ built-in tools.</div>\n   269→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   270→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   271→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   272→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-02</span>\n   273→                </div>\n   274→            </div>\n   275→\n   276→            <div class=\"item\">\n   277→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/mitja-kurath/daniel\" target=\"_blank\">Daniel</a></div>\n   278→                <div class=\"item-description\">The proactive AI software engineer that lives in your terminal. Navigates directories, executes commands, fixes bugs across multiple files, and manages development lifecycle autonomously.</div>\n   279→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   280→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   281→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   282→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-02</span>\n   283→                </div>\n   284→            </div>\n   285→\n   286→            <div class=\"item\">\n   287→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/cry-nix/MultiCode\" target=\"_blank\">MultiCode</a></div>\n   288→                <div class=\"item-description\">Terminal AI coding buddy that reads files, edits code, and runs commands. Free and open-source alternative to Claude Code working with any model via OpenRouter.</div>\n   289→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   290→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   291→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   292→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-02</span>\n   293→                </div>\n   294→            </div>\n   295→\n   296→            <div class=\"item\">\n   297→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/prithvi-45/memforge\" target=\"_blank\">memforge</a></div>\n   298→                <div class=\"item-description\">Persistent memory MCP server for AI coding agents. Install once, your agents never forget. Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf, Aider.</div>\n   299→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   300→                    <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   301→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   302→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-02</span>\n   303→                </div>\n   304→            </div>\n   305→\n   306→            <div class=\"item\">\n   307→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Peter08091996/waifu-code\" target=\"_blank\">Waifu Code</a></div>\n   308→                <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source anime-style AI terminal coding assistant. Brings a unique aesthetic to terminal-based AI coding assistance.</div>\n   309→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   310→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   311→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   312→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-02</span>\n   313→                </div>\n   314→            </div>\n   315→\n   316→            <div class=\"item\">\n   317→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/MauricioPerera/oxshell\" target=\"_blank\">OxShell</a></div>\n   318→                <div class=\"item-description\">AI coding assistant for the terminal powered by Cloudflare Workers AI and minimemory, built in Rust. Can read files, write code, run commands, and orchestrate multiple agents.</div>\n   319→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   320→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   321→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   322→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-01</span>\n   323→                </div>\n   324→            </div>\n   325→\n   326→            <div class=\"item\">\n   327→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/albertgd/free-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\">Free Claude Code</a></div>\n   328→                <div class=\"item-description\">AI coding assistant for the terminal that works exactly like Claude Code but connects to Groq (free tier), OpenAI, or Google Gemini instead of Anthropic's API.</div>\n   329→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   330→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   331→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   332→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-01</span>\n   333→                </div>\n   334→            </div>\n   335→\n   336→            <div class=\"item\">\n   337→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/tienedev/claude-code-nix\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code Nix</a></div>\n   338→                <div class=\"item-description\">Nix flake for Claude Code providing AI coding assistant in your terminal with auto-updated daily builds and reproducible Nix-based installation.</div>\n   339→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   340→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   341→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   342→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-01</span>\n   343→                </div>\n   344→            </div>\n   345→\n   346→            <div class=\"item\">\n   347→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/pookieclaw/camel-code\" target=\"_blank\">Camel Code</a></div>\n   348→                <div class=\"item-description\">Terminal AI coding assistant written in OCaml combining functional programming robustness with modern AI capabilities for a unique 'two humps, zero runtime' approach.</div>\n   349→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   350→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   351→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   352→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-01</span>\n   353→                </div>\n   354→            </div>\n   355→\n   356→            <div class=\"item\">\n   357→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/0x94t3z/mini-codex\" target=\"_blank\">Mini Codex</a></div>\n   358→                <div class=\"item-description\">Terminal coding assistant with workspace-scoped file tools and multi-provider support (Gemini, OpenAI, OpenRouter, xAI). Lightweight alternative for AI-assisted coding.</div>\n   359→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   360→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   361→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   362→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-04-01</span>\n   363→                </div>\n   364→            </div>\n   365→\n   366→            <div class=\"item\">\n   367→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/kepinski85/kempa-ai-devbox\" target=\"_blank\">Kempa AI Devbox</a></div>\n   368→                <div class=\"item-description\">A self-hosted AI learning and building environment designed for Raspberry Pi, featuring multi-agent workflow for teaching programming and collaborating on projects.</div>\n   369→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   370→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   371→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   372→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-31</span>\n   373→                </div>\n   374→            </div>\n   375→\n   376→            <div class=\"item\">\n   377→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/nickleodoen/RewindAI\" target=\"_blank\">RewindAI</a></div>\n   378→                <div class=\"item-description\">VS Code extension that gives AI coding agents version-controlled memory. Chat, commit, checkout — the agent remembers. Powered by Neo4j knowledge graph.</div>\n   379→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   380→                    <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   381→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   382→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-30</span>\n   383→                </div>\n   384→            </div>\n   385→\n   386→            <div class=\"item\">\n   387→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/AmanTShekar/zenith-terminal-buddy\" target=\"_blank\">Zenith Terminal Buddy</a></div>\n   388→                <div class=\"item-description\">An interactive AI-powered pet mascot for VS Code that monitors terminal output to automatically catch and explain errors before you even have to ask.</div>\n   389→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   390→                    <span class=\"tag\">IDE-integrated tool</span>\n   391→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   392→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-30</span>\n   393→                </div>\n   394→            </div>\n   395→\n   396→            <div class=\"item\">\n   397→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Rabba-Meghana/codebase-autocomplete-plugin\" target=\"_blank\">Codebase Autocomplete Plugin</a></div>\n   398→                <div class=\"item-description\">Codebase-aware AI autocomplete plugin for JetBrains IDEs using RAG, Groq, and ChromaDB. Provides intelligent code suggestions based on your entire codebase context.</div>\n   399→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   400→                    <span class=\"tag\">IDE-integrated tool</span>\n   401→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   402→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-30</span>\n   403→                </div>\n   404→            </div>\n   405→\n   406→            <div class=\"item\">\n   407→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/zabarich/danucode\" target=\"_blank\">Danucode</a></div>\n   408→                <div class=\"item-description\">The simplest agent shell for your own models. Backend-agnostic terminal coding agent supporting Ollama, llama.cpp, vLLM, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.</div>\n   409→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   410→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   411→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   412→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-29</span>\n   413→                </div>\n   414→            </div>\n   415→\n   416→            <div class=\"item\">\n   417→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/nitkr/clean-sweep-cortex\" target=\"_blank\">Clean Sweep Cortex</a></div>\n   418→                <div class=\"item-description\">A terminal-based AI coding agent specifically designed to help with cleaning WordPress malwares. Combines code analysis with security-focused workflows.</div>\n   419→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   420→                    <span class=\"tag\">workflow-specific tool</span>\n   421→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   422→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-29</span>\n   423→                </div>\n   424→            </div>\n   425→\n   426→            <div class=\"item\">\n   427→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/ExuberantWitness/openclaw-workspace-version-control\" target=\"_blank\">OpenClaw Workspace Version Control</a></div>\n   428→                <div class=\"item-description\">Safe memory management and rollback for AI agents with version-controlled memory system.</div>\n   429→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   430→                    <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   431→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   432→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-29</span>\n   433→                </div>\n   434→            </div>\n   435→\n   436→            <div class=\"item\">\n   437→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/luminexo/trust\" target=\"_blank\">Trust</a></div>\n   438→                <div class=\"item-description\">A shared terminal environment for pair programming with AI agents. Built with Rust, it provides a terminal-based IDE environment for collaborative AI-assisted programming.</div>\n   439→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   440→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   441→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   442→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-28</span>\n   443→                </div>\n   444→            </div>\n   445→\n   446→            <div class=\"item\">\n   447→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Swofty-Developments/CodeForge\" target=\"_blank\">CodeForge</a></div>\n   448→                <div class=\"item-description\">An AI code editor that wraps Claude Code and Codex into a native desktop application with multi-thread sessions, an embedded browser, and a sleek dark UI.</div>\n   449→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   450→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   451→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   452→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-27</span>\n   453→                </div>\n   454→            </div>\n   455→\n   456→            <div class=\"item\">\n   457→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/zdenham/anvil\" target=\"_blank\">Anvil</a></div>\n   458→                <div class=\"item-description\">A desktop IDE designed specifically for parallel agent work. Enables isolated worktrees for parallel development without merge conflicts with first-class spec support.</div>\n   459→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   460→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n   461→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   462→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-25</span>\n   463→                </div>\n   464→            </div>\n   465→\n   466→            <div class=\"item\">\n   467→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/JayCodesX/orager\" target=\"_blank\">Orager</a></div>\n   468→                <div class=\"item-description\">Production-grade AI agent runtime and CLI built as the runtime behind Paperclip agents. Features multi-turn tool-calling, persistent memory, and multi-agent orchestration.</div>\n   469→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   470→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   471→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   472→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-24</span>\n   473→                </div>\n   474→            </div>\n   475→\n   476→            <div class=\"item\">\n   477→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/anYuJia/yode\" target=\"_blank\">Yode</a></div>\n   478→                <div class=\"item-description\">Open-source AI coding agent for your terminal built in Rust. Reads, edits, searches, and runs commands from a single conversation with multi-provider support.</div>\n   479→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   480→                    <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   481→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   482→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-23</span>\n   483→                </div>\n   484→            </div>\n   485→\n   486→            <div class=\"item\">\n   487→                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/zackbrooks84/continuum\" target=\"_blank\">continuum</a></div>\n   488→                <div class=\"item-description\">Async task queue + persistent memory for AI agents that remembers everything, runs tasks while you sleep, and picks up exactly where you left off.</div>\n   489→                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   490→                    <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   491→                    <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   492→                    <span class=\"release-date\">2026-03-23</span>\n   493→                </div>\n   494→            </div>\n   495→        </section>\n   496→\n   497→        <section class=\"column\">\n   498→            <div class=\"column-header\">\n   499→                Whitelist Updates <span class=\"count\">0</span>\n   500→            </div>\n   501→            <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   502→                No whitelist updates available for this period.\n   503→            </div>\n   504→        </section>\n   505→\n   506→        <section class=\"column\">\n   507→            <div class=\"column-header\">\n   508→                Technical Insights <span class=\"count\">0</span>\n   509→            </div>\n   510→            <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   511→                No technical insights available for this period.\n   512→            </div>\n   513→        </section>\n   514→    </main>\n   515→\n   516→    <footer class=\"footer\">\n   517→        <p>\n   518→            <a href=\"#\">Archives</a> |\n   519→            <a href=\"#\">About</a> |\n   520→            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a> |\n   521→            <a href=\"#\">Submit Updates</a>\n   522→        </p>\n   523→        <p style=\"margin-top: 10px;\">\n   524→            Generated by AgentDaily — Tracking the agentic coding revolution\n   525→        </p>\n   526→    </footer>\n   527→</body>\n   528→</html>\n   529→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
